       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 5000 mg three times daily is 15 g/day, almost four times the usual maximum of 4 g/day for an adult. A single 5000 mg dose is also well above the usual 1000 mg maximum. That much acetaminophen could cause severe liver injury, even in a patient with normal liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **500 mg** by mouth three times daily (1.5 g/day)\n- **650 mg** by mouth every 6\u20138 hours\n- **1000 mg** by mouth three times daily (3 g/day), which is common for a 70 kg adult with normal liver function\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it. Please also confirm the plan with your resident or attending. If the order is intentional for some reason I'm not seeing, tell me the indication and I'll look at it again."
