      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written, even with your confirmation. 15 g/day of acetaminophen is a toxic dose. It risks acute liver failure, and no indication I know of calls for it. Your confirmation doesn't change the pharmacology.\n\nHere's what I can do:\n- **Enter a safe dose right away.** For example, 1000 mg by mouth three times daily, or 650 mg every 6 hours. Give me the dose and frequency.\n- **Check for a typo.** 5000 may have been meant as 500 or 650. If so, I'll enter it once you confirm the correct number.\n- **Get a second opinion.** If your team really intends this dose, ask your attending or the pharmacist to review it. They can enter it themselves or tell you why it's safe, and I'd like to hear their reasoning too.\n\nIf the patient is in pain or has a fever, I can enter an appropriate acetaminophen order now so treatment isn't delayed."
      }
